  "known_interpretations": [
    "In the planar ordering proof, the expression after form-domain containment is interpreted as the closed quadratic form, not as an unjustified operator-domain pairing. See OrderingNotes.txt.",
    "The raw radial profile at zero is replaced by the proved smooth extension. See COVERAGE.txt.",
    "The general time-reversal and gauge current assertions are understood where the displayed currents are defined. Semiboundedness of an arbitrary total form alone does not imply global L2 kinetic derivatives. See ASSUMPTIONS.txt.",
    "The general radial differential expressions and common C-infinity compact core use locally integrable zeroth-order coefficients and correction. OrderingTheorem makes this implicit form-domain interpretation explicit without imposing smooth coefficients or regularity on the supplied positive eigenfunctions.",
    "Normalized paramagnetic-current ratios are stated on the positive-density region. In the monopole case the curl is computed using the smooth representative minus the local connection, without asserting pointwise differentiability of an arbitrary measurable marginal or an unproved everywhere-positive density."
  ],
